@startuml
!theme plain
title A2A Deep Link and Unknown Outcome Recovery — Synthetic
actor Payer
participant "Mobile Checkout" as UI
participant "Merchant Backend" as Merchant
participant "Payment Platform" as Platform
participant "Provider Adapter" as Adapter
participant "External Provider" as Provider
participant "Banking App" as Bank
participant "Recovery Worker" as Worker
Payer -> UI : choose bank transfer
UI -> Merchant : request checkout
Merchant -> Platform : create intent
Platform -> Adapter : initiate A2A attempt
Adapter -> Provider : register attempt
Provider --> Adapter : approved app link
Adapter --> Platform : checkout URI + reference
Platform --> Merchant : pending + URI
Merchant --> UI : app link
UI -> Bank : launch approved app link
Payer -> Bank : authenticate and approve
Bank -> Provider : process authorization
Bank --> UI : return to merchant app
note over UI,Platform
Return URL means the user returned, NOT paid.
end note
UI -> Merchant : refresh status
Merchant -> Platform : query intent
Platform --> Merchant : pending/unknown until verified
Provider --> Adapter : callback delivery (may be delayed)
Adapter --> Platform : validated outcome
alt Provider callback absent or uncertain
 Platform -> Worker : schedule enquiry
 Worker -> Adapter : query by external reference
 Adapter -> Provider : provider status API
 Provider --> Adapter : confirmed or pending outcome
 Adapter --> Worker : mapped status
 Worker -> Platform : guarded state transition / reschedule
end
Platform --> Merchant : durable result notification
Merchant --> UI : display authoritative outcome
@enduml